Data sources
------------

JMdict
  Copyright © James William Breen and the Electronic Dictionary Research
  and Development Group (EDRDG). CC-BY-SA 4.0.
  https://www.edrdg.org/jmdict/j_jmdict.html
  https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html
  Read through scriptin/jmdict-simplified
  (https://github.com/scriptin/jmdict-simplified).

Example sentences — the Tatoeba Project
  Japanese example sentences in the seed come from Tatoeba, through
  JMdict's example index (JMdict_e_examp). CC-BY 2.0 France.
  https://tatoeba.org
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/fr/

JLPT vocabulary lists
  Jonathan Waller's JLPT lists (https://www.tanos.co.uk), curated and
  re-emitted by stephenmk/yomitan-jlpt-vocab. CC-BY-SA 4.0.
  https://github.com/stephenmk/yomitan-jlpt-vocab

Word frequency
  The internet-jp frequency list by Serge Sharoff, University of Leeds
  Centre for Translation Studies, as mirrored by hingston/japanese.
  CC BY 2.5. Used to bucket cards into rarity tiers.
  https://github.com/hingston/japanese
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/

Science & Programming pack (packs/science.json)
  Headwords, readings and glosses from the AnkiWeb shared deck
  "Japanese Programming, Math and Science Terms"
  (https://ankiweb.net/shared/info/433387608), which names no author and
  states no licence. Rarity comes from the JMdict-derived data above.
  If you are the deck's author and want different credit or terms,
  please open an issue.


